WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.300 --> 00:00:14.500
Good morning John; it's Friday, January 19th.
I was inspired by your little walk around

00:00:14.500 --> 00:00:17.770
Manhattan in the morning, so I decided to
take a little walk around Missoula in the

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:24.420
morning. Turns out there's no one here! No
nannies and no rich kids, so I can't play

00:00:24.420 --> 00:00:30.360
that game. I can play, like, picnic table,
park bench.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:36.200
The park is completely abandoned, but it's
fun still! So you know this, but none of our

00:00:36.200 --> 00:00:41.781
viewers do. Every year around this time, I
send a survey to all of my friends and family.

00:00:41.781 --> 00:00:45.930
I wonder if all of you are getting nauseous?
That would be awesome!

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:50.059
My friends and family answer that survey,
and then I put it online so everyone can see

00:00:50.059 --> 00:00:51.579
the answers.

00:00:51.579 --> 00:00:55.269
My butt hurts. Jesus, this thing is not built
for my butt!

00:00:55.269 --> 00:01:00.559
The problem is that the survey is text based,
so I can't actually send it to you, but there's

00:01:00.559 --> 00:01:06.320
no way I'm going to break this tradition.
So this year, I'm going to give you the survey

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:08.020
in video blog form!

00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:10.400
Questions one through six are the same as
they've always been, and I already know the

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:13.000
answer to all those questions, so I'm not
going to ask you.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:16.890
We start with question seven: How long have
you known Hank and Katherine?

00:01:16.890 --> 00:01:20.370
Question eight: What do you want from us?

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:25.730
Question nine: What are you doing? Please
be as specific as possible because we actually

00:01:25.730 --> 00:01:27.150
all want to know.

00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:30.220
Question ten: How much longer do you think
you'll be doing it?

00:01:30.220 --> 00:01:34.250
Question eleven: Why are you doing it?

00:01:34.250 --> 00:01:41.310
Question twelve: What do you want to be doing?

00:01:41.310 --> 00:01:45.020
Question thirteen: What is next in your life?

00:01:45.020 --> 00:01:51.860
Question fourteen: How you doin'?

00:01:51.860 --> 00:01:55.350
Question fifteen: What's the best book you
read this year?

00:01:55.350 --> 00:02:02.750
Question sixteen: Describe a perfect day.

00:02:02.750 --> 00:02:08.890
Assuming that all things come to an end, how
will humans go extinct?

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:11.220
So how are you feeling about kids these days?

00:02:11.220 --> 00:02:17.140
In this space, create your own question and
answer it.

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:22.170
Ambrozzo tastes better than any other kind
of food. What does ambrozzo taste like?

00:02:22.170 --> 00:02:25.230
If you were a cliché, what cliché would
you be?

00:02:25.230 --> 00:02:28.460
What's your least favorite part of any given
day?

00:02:28.460 --> 00:02:30.230
Do you enjoy science fiction?

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:36.030
Cheese or chocolate?

00:02:36.030 --> 00:02:38.060
What was your first concert?

00:02:38.060 --> 00:02:41.100
Where would you live if you could live anywhere?

00:02:41.100 --> 00:02:46.020
Would you rather invisibility or time travel?

00:02:46.020 --> 00:02:51.250
If you could start a business that would be
instantly successful, what kind of business

00:02:51.250 --> 00:02:53.340
would it be?

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:55.819
What's wrong with the world?

00:02:55.819 --> 00:02:59.220
And the final question, number thirty: Can
I put this survey on my webpage?

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.319
I didn't get to play nanny nanny rich kid
this morning but there is another game that

00:03:02.319 --> 00:03:06.500
I sometimes play. It's called, Go to Barnes
and Noble and see who's on the young adult

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:07.500
romance shelf.

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:14.040
(singing) Lady, lady, lady; lady, lady, lady,
lady, lady, lady, lady lady, John Green!

00:03:14.040 --> 00:03:20.569
There's nothing wrong with that! That's great,
it's great! You-you're among giants; right

00:03:20.569 --> 00:03:26.630
there in the middle. Tales of love and romance,
no, it's great! I think it's great. Really,

00:03:26.630 --> 00:03:30.530
right there on the end cap, right in the middle.
Tales of love and romance. I think it's great.

00:03:30.530 --> 00:03:33.760
Really, well done. And I'll see you on Monday.

